------------
Introduction
------------
       Offline is a simple program that hasn't been done that many times
before. The idea of offline is when your BBS is offline for any reason you
can run my program and let your users know why the BBS is offline. Offline
is also easy to setup so you need waste no time setting it up which will
give you more time to fix whatever is wrong with your BBS.

------------
Instructions
------------
       A main feature of offline is it is very simple to set up, a couple
of easy questions to answer then your away. If you are finding it difficult
to work heres a quick run down of the options :-

F1 : Wait for incoming calls

This leaves the modem on automatic answer for when someone trys to connect
to your BBS.

F2 : Enter BBS info

It's best to use this option first. What this is for is to enter your BBS
details and who the sysop is and other bits and bobs that the user will
see on login. On this full version there is an option to turn the messages
off, this is incase your HD is invalidated or so knackered nothing can
be saved to it, if your problem is only simple or is nothing to do with
your HD then leave this on as this allows users to leave you messages,
these can be found in the same draw as Offline.

F3 : Instructions/Help

A basic run down of what the commands do.

F10 : Exit to WB

This will exit to workbench while on the title screen.

Amiga & A :

This will allow you to flick between Offline and whatever you are
doing/fixing.

----------------
What you'll need
----------------
       The requirements for this program are an Amiga and a modem, the
serial settings are set to 9600 to be on the safe side, this may not
seem fast but it's fast enough for the program.

-------
Updates
-------
       In the next couple of versions i am hoping to add the feature
save settings, this will allow you to enter your settings then never
have to enter them again unless you want to change them. Also on the
message save bit i might add more commands like continue or edit
a line. Depending on the speed of the modem transfer i may also add
a setting where you can enter your own modem speed, this depends weather
it is needed.

